6,481,1124,11520,37018,90,16,16,15170,23,92,284,220,16,13,18,22,20,59,4292,256,481,1124,11520,37018,90,21,15170,16,21,92,284,1124,37018,90,18,15170,23,92,284,220,15,13,18,22,20,59,49555,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,2610,1231,312,18883,55856,279,3491,323,18130,279,6291,504,279,7167,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{11}{8},\\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$? Express your answer in simplest form.\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo find the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set \\(\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{11}{8}, \\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}\\), we first need to determine the decimal or fractional equivalent of each fraction to compare them easily.\n\n1. **Convert each fraction to a decimal or a simpler fraction:**\n   - \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is approximately \\(0.428571\\ldots\\).\n   - \\(\\frac{4}{3} = 1.333333\\ldots\\).\n   - \\(\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\\).\n   - \\(\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\\).\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"You may re-analyze the problem and rewrite the solution from the beginning.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"837e5b6bc33d42cea18b47d6b670464506e09ad750d49cf670d7680b806513fe"},"seconds":24.3005588054657,"seed":234070600971076160,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{11}{8}, \\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$, we first need to compare the values of each fraction. \n\n1. Simplify the fractions where possible:\n   - $\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8}$ since both the numerator and the denominator can be divided by 2.\n\n2. Compare the simplified fractions:\n   - $\\frac{3}{7}$\n   - $\\frac{4}{3}$\n   - $\\frac{11}{8}$\n   - $\\frac{3}{8}$\n\n3. Convert the fractions to have a common denominator to compare them directly, or compare their approximate decimal values:\n   - $\\frac{3}{7} \\approx 0.4286$\n   - $\\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.3333$\n   - $\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375$\n   - $\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375$\n\nFrom the decimal approximations, we can see that:\n- The smallest value is $\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375$.\n- The largest value is $\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375$.\n\n4. Calculate the positive difference between the greatest and the least member:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{11}{8}, \\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$, we first need to compare the values of each fraction. \n\n1. Simplify the fractions where possible:\n   - $\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8}$ since both the numerator and the denominator can be divided by 2.\n\n2. Compare the simplified fractions:\n   - $\\frac{3}{7}$\n   - $\\frac{4}{3}$\n   - $\\frac{11}{8}$\n   - $\\frac{3}{8}$\n\n3. Convert the fractions to have a common denominator to compare them directly, or compare their approximate decimal values:\n   - $\\frac{3}{7} \\approx 0.4286$\n   - $\\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.3333$\n   - $\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375$\n   - $\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375$\n\nFrom the decimal approximations, we can see that:\n- The smallest value is $\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375$.\n- The largest value is $\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375$.\n\n4. Calculate the positive difference between the greatest and the least member:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).","id":"prealgebra:855"}
